{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106918","id":2550753233,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6YCWfR","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106918","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106918.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106918.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106918","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106918/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106918/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106918/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b3ddb8803594191338078925bd8e1e45bdde62f3","number":106918,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix Area3D signal emissions when using Jolt Physics","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #106629.\r\nAllows for #105746.\r\n\r\nThis pull request adds reference counting of the shape index pairs that are managed in `JoltArea3D`, and changes its event emitting of `PhysicsServer3D::AREA_BODY_ADDED` and `PhysicsServer3D::AREA_BODY_REMOVED` to instead only happen when this reference counter gets set to/from zero.\r\n\r\nThis is necessary due to triangle-based shapes like ConcavePolygonShape3D (and presumably HeightMapShape3D) currently being able to produce multiple contacts/overlaps/manifolds for different triangles, that all have different Jolt sub-shape pairs, but that resolve down to the same shape index pair, which I failed to take into account when first implementing support for Area3D, resulting in it emitting events when it shouldn't.\r\n\r\nThis reference counting will also come in handy for #105746, which I believe should make the above mentioned multiple contacts/overlaps/manifolds non-existent, but which should still benefit from this reference counting for managing the moving of the single contact/overlap/manifold as it moves between different triangles.\r\n\r\nThis pull request also fixes an issue where removing or adding shapes to a body that's overlapping with an Area3D would similarly result in borked signal emissions, which turned out to be part me having screwed up `JoltContactListener3D::_flush_area_shifts` when first implementing Area3D support and part regression from #101189.\r\n\r\nNote however that there is still a slight discrepancy in how these signal emissions happen when comparing with Godot Physics. For example, if you have a RigidBody3D with three shapes that's enveloped by an Area3D, and you remove the middle one, Godot Physics will emit two exit events, one for index 1 and one for index 2, and then an enter event for index 1. With Jolt, as of this pull request, you will instead only get a single event, which is the exit event for index 2.\r\n\r\nIt might be worth taking a closer look at that discrepancy at some later point, but I don't think it needs to prevent this PR from being merged.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"created_at":"2024-12-19T08:5